:News_ActiveDutyMilitaryScholarship a wsu:NewsArticle ;
    rdfs:label "Wright State University launches new undergraduate scholarship for active-duty military" ;
    rdfs:comment "June 10, 2025. Active-duty military members, activated Guard members and reservists can pursue a bachelor's degree with support from the new Active Duty Military Undergraduate Scholarship." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://webapp2.wright.edu/web1/newsroom/2025/06/10/wright-state-university-launches-new-undergraduate-scholarship-for-active-duty-military/> .

:News_ScherzingerTonyAward a wsu:NewsArticle ;
    rdfs:label "Wright State alum Nicole Scherzinger wins first Tony Award for starring role in 'Sunset Boulevard'" ;
    rdfs:comment "June 9, 2025. Nicole Scherzinger, who studied musical theatre and acting at Wright State, received the Tony Award for best leading actress in a musical." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://webapp2.wright.edu/web1/newsroom/2025/06/09/wright-state-alum-nicole-scherzinger-wins-first-tony-award-for-sunset-boulevard-performance/> .

:News_MediaHighlightsJune1to6 a wsu:NewsArticle ;
    rdfs:label "Wright State media highlights, June 1–6" ;
    rdfs:comment "June 6, 2025. Coverage of a historic NCAA upset, consumer behavior expertise, a new academic partnership in health care, and a semiconductor internship program." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://webapp2.wright.edu/web1/newsroom/2025/06/06/wright-state-media-highlights-june-1-6/> .

:News_MBAPrincetonReview2026 a wsu:NewsArticle ;
    rdfs:label "Wright State MBA earns national recognition as one of The Princeton Review's Best On-Campus Programs" ;
    rdfs:comment "August 31, 2026." .

:News_GlobalRankings2026 a wsu:NewsArticle ;
    rdfs:label "Global rankings place Wright State among the world's top universities" ;
    rdfs:comment "June 05, 2026." .


# ==== Facts ====

:Fact_NamedForWrightBrothers a wsu:Fact ;
    rdfs:label "Named for the Wright brothers" ;
    rdfs:comment "Wright State University was named to honor aviation pioneers Orville and Wilbur Wright, who invented the world's first successful airplane in their Dayton bicycle shop." .

:Fact_PublicArt a wsu:Fact ;
    rdfs:label "Public art on campus" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Wright State campus features artistic pieces both in- and outdoors; more public art will be added as structures are renovated and new buildings constructed." .

:Fact_TunnelSystem a wsu:Fact ;
    rdfs:label "Pedestrian tunnel system" ;
    rdfs:comment "Nearly two miles of tunnels (10,436 feet) beneath the Dayton campus link 21 of 22 buildings in the academic section; believed to be one of the most extensive collegiate pedestrian tunnel systems in the United States." .

:Fact_CampusFacilities a wsu:Fact ;
    rdfs:label "Campus facilities" ;
    rdfs:comment "32 academic buildings on 730 acres across two campuses." .

:Fact_AlumniNetwork a wsu:Fact ;
    rdfs:label "Alumni network" ;
    rdfs:comment "More than 111,000 Wright State alumni." .


